		<#macro rollerChecklistBCC>
		
		  <table class="checklist">
		    <tr>
		      <td colspan="2"><b>Door Curtain</b></td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check general condition of door curtain.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check slats for sign of wear or damage.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check wind locks if secured.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check that end-locks fixed to the ends of the slat are secure.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check curtain is securely fixed to barrel assembly.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check the operation of any locking devise fitted.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check bottom rail and seal for wear or damage.</td>
		      <td>&nbsp;</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td colspan="2">* if bottom rail is bowed or bent to minor degree such that it can be straightened without removing the rail, straighten as required</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td colspan="2"><b>Side Guides</b></td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check all fixings are secure.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check condition of guide channel and straighten any slight deformities.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Grease guide channel if required.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check guide stops at high level.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check any chain lock fitted.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check that the door curtain feeds into the guides smoothly and correctly.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td colspan="2"><b>End Plates and Drum</b></td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check fixings are secure.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check &amp; tighten hand chain wheel assembly - Planetary Gear or Direct Drive.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check drum, axle, bearings &amp; liners for signs of wear.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check, adjust &amp; lubricate transmission chain and drive sprocket.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check and lubricate all gearing.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check and tighten gear box fixings and motor brake operation.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check all grub screws and keys.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check and minor adjustment to spring tension if required, balance the door curtain.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td colspan="2"><b>Electrical Drive System</b></td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check motor is securely fixed.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check the drive gearing and lubricate.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check operation of manual override system.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check electrical cables &amp; control box condition and PE safety beam operation.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check if an isolating switch is fitted within easy reach.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check "Dead man Down" operation and check and adjust limit switches.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td>[ ] Check condition of UPS system.</td>
		      <td>[ ] Check any other control systems if installed.</td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td colspan="2"><b>Service Label</b></td>
		    </tr>
		    <tr>
		      <td colspan="2">[ ] Complete the service label adhered to the door and logbook if available</td>
